  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the number of sales that Tomas completed:\n\n$$\n912⟶900\n$$\n\nThe ratio of Rachel's sales to Tomas's sales is\n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{9}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents Rachel's sales  and the denominator represents Tomas's sales.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $900$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $100$:\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 100}{9\\times 100}=\\frac{700}{900}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, Rachel completed approximately $700$ sales.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
